  &= \frac{6\sqrt{3}}{sin(30^{\circ}) * 3} + 6\sqrt{3} + \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
  &= 4\sqrt{3} + \frac{3}{2} + 6\sqrt{3} + \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
  &= 8\sqrt{3} + \frac{9\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
  &= \boxed{\frac{48\sqrt{3} + 9}{2}} \text{ feet}
\end{align*}

And finally, we can find the sum of the edge lengths of the pyramid by counting the six edges of the hexagonal base and the three lateral edges:

