Now, we can calculate the area of the trapezoid using the formula: Area = 1/2 * base * height. Since AB (fourth side of the trapezoid) is also the sum of the bases (first and third sides), we can calculate the area as Area = 1/2 * (18+0) * 4 = 72 square units.

